            <ArticleTitle>[Psychic pain, somatic risks and psychological suffering in elderly people].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>37-40</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Physical pain, like psychic pain, is still trivialised by healthcare practitioners working in geriatrics. Physical pains in elderly people are not isolated but often occur in a context of motor and mental incapacities rendering communication of the complaint somewhat erratic. They generate anxiety, which often amplifies their perception. This article represents a reflection about the management of pain in elderly people.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
